      "order": 6,
      "bbox": [
        271,
        167,
        301,
        891
      ],
      "margin_number": 5,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "οὐκ ἐάσας What is this? Compare it with εἴασας. Remember that the aorist\nindicative has an augment. The participle has not.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_entry",
      "order": 7,
      "bbox": [
        311,
        168,
        401,
        878
      ],
      "margin_number": 7,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "πιθέσθαι Aorist infinitive from ἐπιθόμην (second aorist of πείθομαι). For\naorist infinitives see GE pp. 187–189, #195–197. Here the aorist is used to\nemphasise the aspect. ‘You must (χρή) stay here (present infinitive =\nall the time, a process) and obey me [now] (aorist infinitive denotes a single\nevent).’",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_entry",
      "order": 8,
      "bbox": [
        409,
        168,
        442,
        580
      ],
      "margin_number": 10,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "δικάσαι First aorist infinitive active from δικάζω.\nδυνήσῃ The future of δύναμαι: ‘you will be able’.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_entry",
      "order": 9,
      "bbox": [
        445,
        159,
        482,
        895
      ],
      "margin_number": 11,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "μοι ... ἐνθάδε μένοντι Note the agreement: ‘How will it be possible for me\nremaining here to be a juror?’ ‘How will it be possible ... if I stay here?’",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
