        524,
        159,
        537,
        579
      ],
      "margin_number": 16,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "παύσασθαι First aorist infinitive middle.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_entry",
      "order": 12,
      "bbox": [
        542,
        157,
        595,
        856
      ],
      "margin_number": 17,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "κατάσκοπον κατά, σκοπέω. Cf. the various English ‘-scope’ words. Most\nrelevant here is ‘episcopal’, from ἐπίσκοπος an ‘overseer’ or a ‘bishop’ in\nChristian Greek.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_entry",
      "order": 13,
      "bbox": [
        600,
        192,
        615,
        755
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "γενέσθαι What is this? What are the principal parts of γίγνομαι?",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_entry",
      "order": 14,
      "bbox": [
        619,
        158,
        654,
        891
      ],
      "margin_number": 19,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "ἐξευρεῖν What is it? Try the principal parts of εὑρίσκω. Remember that the\ninfinitive does not have an augment.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
